lisa-design:
PR A (lean plan): the ca package and interception in one PR. No gatewayca step, no rotation, no name-constraint drift check on Load (deferred). Generate/Load/LoadOrGenerate take a context (AGENTS.md: I/O takes a context), a departure from the LLD's ca.Load(dir). No credential injection here: intercepted requests are forwarded with every carrier stripped and the class's cookie rule; PRs B and C set the credential in forwardIntercepted's Rewrite after stripCarriers. Tests reach their TLS upstream through Gateway.upstreamPort (443 by default), since a test can't bind 443.
